    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n12851" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">dēlăpĭdo</span></b> ,
			āre, v. a. * <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>To clear from stones</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">locum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cato R.
					R. 46, 1</span></i>
			.—* </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>To lay with stones, to pave</i>: DELAPIDATA lapide
			strata, Paul. ex <i><span class="en">Fest. p. 73, 13</span></i> Müll.;
			cf.: DELAPIDATA, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λιθόστρωτα</span>,
		Gloss.</div>
